 and then one for graduate study at the University of Chicago pulled him out of the close family circle. While he was away, the industries that supported the town failed, and drug dealing rushed in to fill the economic void. News of arrests and premature deaths among Brent's childhood friends underscored the precariousness of his perch in a world of mostly white achievers. A younger brother became a cocaine dealer and was murdered by one of his \"clients.\" His death propelled Brent into a reconsideration of his childhood and coming-of-age that offers vivid portraits of family and place, of values that supported and pressures that tore apart, of the appeal and pain of entering a predominantly white world, and of the strengths and vulnerabilities of the black world he grew away from.","publicationYear":1994,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"African Americans","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-parallel-time-growing-up-in-black-and-white-brent-staples"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-parallel-time-growing-up-in-black-and-white-brent-staples"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Journalists","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-parallel-time-growing-up-in-black-and-white-brent-staples"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Newspaper editors","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-parallel-time-growing-up-in-black-and-white-brent-staples"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"New York Times reviewed","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-parallel-time-growing-up-in-black-and-white-brent-staples"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Race relations","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-parallel-time-growing-up-in-black-and-white-brent-staples"}],"displaySummary":"For Brent Staples there is the added dimens